WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.071 --> 00:00:14.522
"How's that?" Ally asked as she finished hanging a model of Earth's solar system from the ceiling.

2
00:00:14.523 --> 00:00:19.796
"Great!" Mateo said. "We're ready for our grand reopening!"

3
00:00:19.797 --> 00:00:24.862
"Not if Kate doesn't get back with the new menus," Ray said.

4
00:00:24.863 --> 00:00:29.783
"She just texted me," Bethany said. "She'll be here soon."

5
00:00:29.784 --> 00:00:37.021
Ally gulped. She'd been relieved when the diner had closed for a week to prepare for the reopening.

6
00:00:37.022 --> 00:00:43.099
There'd been no chance of Dr. Lloyd coming in with his granddaughter.

7
00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:48.104
But today was a different story. The two of them could enter at any moment.

8
00:00:48.105 --> 00:00:51.199
"Guess it's time to fire up the grill," Ray said.

9
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:55.431
When Ally looked at him, she thought she saw tears in his eyes.

10
00:00:55.432 --> 00:00:58.044
"Thank you for all your help," he said.

11
00:00:58.045 --> 00:01:03.300
"I couldn't have done it without you. Especially you, Ally."

12
00:01:03.301 --> 00:01:07.697
"You're the one who makes the delicious food," she said.

13
00:01:07.698 --> 00:01:10.675
"New menus, hot off the press!"

14
00:01:10.676 --> 00:01:15.072
Kate came running in the back door and handed a menu to everyone.

15
00:01:15.073 --> 00:01:19.000
"The Cosmic Omelet sounds great," Bethany said.

16
00:01:19.001 --> 00:01:23.092
"So does the Beta Burgana!" Mateo said with a grin.

17
00:01:23.093 --> 00:01:30.859
Ally glanced at the main door. "It's time to open up."

18
00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:34.662
But when Mateo unlocked the door, no one was waiting to come in.

19
00:01:34.663 --> 00:01:38.113
The street out front was completely deserted.

20
00:01:38.114 --> 00:01:43.763
Ray came out of the kitchen, wringing his apron. "No one's here."

21
00:01:43.764 --> 00:01:47.169
"Don't worry, Papi, they'll come," Mateo said.

22
00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:52.962
"Uh-oh," Ally thought. But only seconds later, something amazing happened.

23
00:01:52.963 --> 00:01:56.770
A large bus with the words Space Life Tours pulled up.

24
00:01:56.771 --> 00:02:01.163
The door to the bus opened, and a large group of humans began to pile out.

25
00:02:01.164 --> 00:02:03.413
The bus driver introduced herself.

26
00:02:03.414 --> 00:02:07.972
"We run buses full of tourists every day to the UFO museum.

27
00:02:07.973 --> 00:02:13.905
We read Gourmet Greta's review and decided to bring our passengers here instead of Pepe's.

28
00:02:13.906 --> 00:02:16.842
I hope that's all right with you folks."

29
00:02:16.843 --> 00:02:23.706
"It's fantastic!" Ally said.

30
00:02:23.707 --> 00:02:26.063
The diner got busier by the hour.

31
00:02:26.064 --> 00:02:31.748
Carloads of people kept arriving, saying they'd read the review and couldn't wait to try the food.

32
00:02:31.749 --> 00:02:37.034
"Gourmet Greta has never steered us wrong," said one customer after the other.

33
00:02:37.035 --> 00:02:42.622
Mateo, Kate, and Bethany all jumped in to help take orders and clear tables.

34
00:02:42.623 --> 00:02:46.982
Ally looked around the packed dining room.

35
00:02:46.983 --> 00:02:49.900
"I'm glad I didn't give up," she thought.

36
00:02:49.901 --> 00:02:56.700
"After I buy the fuel and parts, I'll go home knowing I've accomplished something important."

37
00:02:56.701 --> 00:03:02.802
Late in the afternoon, things were quiet enough for Ally to take a break.

38
00:03:02.803 --> 00:03:06.270
"This would look so good on you!"

39
00:03:06.271 --> 00:03:13.120
Kate showed Ally an outfit on her phone.

40
00:03:13.121 --> 00:03:17.114
"You should totally buy it."

41
00:03:17.115 --> 00:03:25.032
"I can't. I have to save money for parts and . . . Never mind!"

42
00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:34.171
Before Kate could ask what she meant, an older man who wore glasses and had a stern expression walked in.

43
00:03:34.172 --> 00:03:38.117
"Welcome to Ray's," Ally greeted him.

44
00:03:38.118 --> 00:03:41.723
"Would you like to sit in a booth or at the counter?"

45
00:03:41.724 --> 00:03:45.821
The man peered at her.

46
00:03:45.822 --> 00:03:49.744
"I didn't come to eat. I came to see you.

47
00:03:49.745 --> 00:03:57.213
My granddaughter, Pearl, insisted that I come here and see you myself."

48
00:03:57.214 --> 00:03:59.768
He handed Ally his business card:

49
00:03:59.769 --> 00:04:01.865
Dr. Cosmo Lloyd

50
00:04:01.866 --> 00:04:04.009
Alien Life Expert

51
00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:09.418
Ally's heart began to race. "What should I do?" she thought.

52
00:04:09.419 --> 00:04:13.319
"I can't escape because my pod needs fuel.

53
00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:16.932
I'll just have to surrender and hope he treats me well."

54
00:04:16.933 --> 00:04:23.322
Ally sighed. "You've found out my true identity. So . . ."

55
00:04:23.323 --> 00:04:26.023
She held her hands out for him to handcuff her.

56
00:04:26.024 --> 00:04:31.253
But Dr. Lloyd burst into loud laughter.

57
00:04:31.254 --> 00:04:34.689
"Pearl told me you were very funny, and she was right.

58
00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:41.184
I came to ask if I can have my weekly meetings of the Sandville Astronomy Club here.

59
00:04:41.185 --> 00:04:45.681
There are about twenty of us, and we'd come every Wednesday."

60
00:04:45.682 --> 00:04:54.444
"Oh!" Ally was delighted. "Of course! I mean if Ray says it's okay!"

61
00:04:54.445 --> 00:05:01.002
Ray stepped forward to shake Dr. Lloyd's hand. "It would be my pleasure."

62
00:05:01.003 --> 00:05:06.647
That night Ally went to her pod and counted up all the money she'd earned so far.

63
00:05:06.648 --> 00:05:11.102
"Alpha, I've earned almost enough money for fuel and parts."

64
00:05:11.103 --> 00:05:17.712
"Goal will soon be accomplished," the computer replied.

65
00:05:17.713 --> 00:05:22.189
It went silent for a second before a blue light started blinking.

66
00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:25.656
"Detecting unhappiness."

67
00:05:25.657 --> 00:05:29.092
"Yes . . ." Ally sighed.

68
00:05:29.093 --> 00:05:33.263
"I mean, I'm happy that I've done so many good deeds for humans.

69
00:05:33.264 --> 00:05:37.561
That'll prove to my parents that I'm ready for a real mission.

70
00:05:37.562 --> 00:05:42.121
But I'll be sad to leave Earth. I kind of like it here."

71
00:05:42.122 --> 00:05:47.317
"Advice: play favorite song," the computer said.

72
00:05:47.318 --> 00:06:16.898
"Great idea!" Ally jumped up and danced her sadness away.

